Aggressive Budget Reallocation to Top-Tier Channels: Immediately shift budget away from the four lower-performing channels (Email, Google Ads, Instagram, YouTube) to Website and Facebook.
Implement a Dual-Segment Targeting Strategy: Differentiate targeting based on cluster value:
Volume Focus (Cluster 0): Direct high-volume campaigns toward the Highest Conversion segment (Cluster 0) using your high-ROI channels.
Value Focus (Cluster 1): Focus on high-LTV (Lifetime Value) and premium upsells for the Highest ROI segment (Cluster 1)
Validate Spend Shift with Formal A/B Testing: Do not roll out the full budget reallocation at once. Launch a controlled A/B test in a specific market or product category, comparing the Recommended Allocation (Treatment) against the current balanced spend (Control) to validate the projected ROI uplift before full scaling.
Personalize Creative for Maximum Engagement: Prioritize the development and A/B testing of highly personalized ad creative/copy specifically designed for the Cluster 0 (High Engagement) segment on the top channels (Website/Facebook) to drive immediate uplift in conversion rate.
Establish Marginal ROI (mROI) Monitoring: Implement an executive dashboard that tracks Marginal ROI per channel continuously. This is crucial for identifying the point of diminishing returns and preventing overspending on a channel as its volume is scaled.
Test Cost Reduction on Low Performers: Utilize the lowest-performing segments (Cluster 2) and channels as testing grounds for cost-efficiency experiments. Test strategies like lower bid caps or frequency limits to determine the minimal viable spend required to maintain baseline awareness while freeing up maximum budget.
